FISH TANK 3D — REPRODUCTION SPECIFICATION
Single-file Python / Pygame application
Use this document to reimplement the program from scratch.

================================================================
1. PURPOSE
================================================================
A real-time 2.5D aquarium. Fish swim in X, Y, and Z (toward /
away from the glass). The tank is viewed either as muted
grayscale 2.5D or as anaglyph stereo (red/green or red/blue
glasses). The user can resize the window, randomize the tank,
swap anaglyph eye colors, and optionally play a music file.

================================================================
2. RUNTIME / FILES
================================================================
Language: Python 3
Library:  pygame 2.x (display, events, transform, surfarray,
          optional mixer.music)
One file: fishtank.py
Optional sidecar written at runtime:
  fishtank_window.json   next to the script
  { "w": int, "h": int, "x": int|null, "y": int|null }

Launch:
  python3 fishtank.py
  python3 fishtank.py --song path/to/file.mp3   (or .wav/.ogg)

No generated sound effects. Mixer is initialized ONLY if
--song is passed. On load failure, print to stderr and continue
silent.

================================================================
3. WINDOW
================================================================
Default size 1280×720, caption "Fish Tank 3D", RESIZABLE.
Minimum size 640×360.

On startup, if fishtank_window.json exists, restore w/h.
If x and y are present, set SDL_VIDEO_WINDOW_POS before
set_mode.

On VIDEORESIZE and on quit, save current w/h to that JSON.
Do NOT use pygame._sdl2 Window APIs (they segfault on some
macOS pygame builds). Position save is best-effort only.

60 FPS. Clamp dt to ≤ 0.05s.

No on-screen HUD, labels, or help text. Controls are
keyboard-only.

================================================================
4. CONTROLS
================================================================
ESC or window close     quit (save window size)
T                       cycle view mode:
                          NORMAL → ANAGLYPH_RG → ANAGLYPH_RB → NORMAL
Y                       swap which eye buffer is packed into
                        red vs green/blue
X                       rebuild a new random tank (fish + decor)

================================================================
5. COORDINATES AND DEPTH
================================================================
Screen: +X right, +Y down, origin top-left.
World also has z:
  z_near = 0.15   closer to viewer / front glass
  z_far  = 1.00   back of tank

Sprite scale (bigger when closer):
  z_scale(z) = lerp(1.55, 0.45, (z - z_near)/(z_far - z_near))

Parallax (anaglyph only), in pixels:
  closeness = saturate((z_far - z)/(z_far - z_near))
  if closeness < 0.12: disparity = 0
  else: disparity = round(closeness^2 * strength)
  strength ≈ 14 at 1280px wide; scale with width if desired.

Eye signs (default, uncrossed):
  LEFT  x' = x + (-1)*disparity
  RIGHT x' = x + (+1)*disparity

NEAR objects split MORE. FAR objects split LITTLE or not at all.
Never invert that mapping.

Z-order is mandatory: collect all drawables, sort by z
DESCENDING (far first), draw so near occludes far.
Do this independently in each eye buffer.
Segmented objects (kelp, lava) use per-segment z.

================================================================
6. COLOR
================================================================
All scene drawing is grayscale, including NORMAL mode.

Y = 0.299R + 0.587G + 0.114B
Then clamp Y to [36, 195].
Never emit (0,0,0) or anything above (195,195,195).
No (250,250,250). “White” ceiling is (195,195,195).

Visual language matches a muted grouper:
  body mid olive-gray ≈ (72,108,78) → luma
  dark ≈ (48,64,50)
  accent ≈ (168,150,78)
All fish species use that family with only a small luma shift
so they remain distinguishable but not colorful.

Water background: vertical gray gradient ≈ 42 → 78.
Sand band at bottom ≈ 36px, mid gray-olive.

ANAGLYPH pack (after two gray eye renders):
  RG:  FINAL.R = LEFT.Y    FINAL.G = RIGHT.Y    FINAL.B = 0
  RB:  FINAL.R = LEFT.Y    FINAL.G = 0          FINAL.B = RIGHT.Y
If swap_filters: exchange LEFT and RIGHT buffers before pack.
Implement pack by copying channels into a new surface
(pygame.surfarray.array3d / make_surface). Do not use
BLEND_ADD / BLEND_RGBA_MULT onto the display surface
(macOS pygame 2.6 has segfaulted on that path).

NORMAL: draw once, eye_sign = 0, gray only, present.

Offscreen eye buffers: opaque RGB, cleared to ≈ (48,48,48),
same pixel size as the window. .convert() is fine; avoid
fullscreen SRCALPHA eye plates.

================================================================
7. FISH
================================================================
Kinds: angelfish, tang, grouper, goldfish, guppy, seahorse.
Procedural sprites (polygons/ellipses), cached per kind.
Sprites are authored nose-LEFT. Flip horizontally when
heading has cos(heading) ≥ 0 so the nose leads motion.

Size multipliers:
  grouper 1.35, guppy and “small angelfish” 0.55,
  seahorse 0.70, others 1.0.
Then multiply by z_scale(z).

Each fish has:
  x, y, z, heading, desired_heading, pitch, desired_pitch,
  speed, max_speed, drag, vx, vy, vz, desired_vz,
  wag_timer, wagging, wag_amp, arc_timer, hunt_cooldown,
  alive, kind, optional flock/leader/slot/small_angel.

Locomotion:
  Speed decays: speed *= exp(-drag * dt).
  When speed < cruise (≈ 28% of max, 20% for seahorse) the
  tail wags: short burst impulse, wag_amp rises, then coasts.
  Heading chases desired_heading with a limited turn rate
  (grouper slower, flock followers faster).
  Every 1.4–3.8s pick a new desired_heading / pitch / vz so
  paths are ARCS, not straight lines.
  Pitch tilts the sprite (seahorse tilt × 0.28, stay upright).
  Bounce z at z_near/z_far (flip vz). Clamp y to keep fish
  in the water column.

Offscreen:
  If x or y leaves a generous margin, the fish is removed.
  Spawn a replacement from a random edge (left/right/top/bottom)
  already facing inward. Keep a target population of 16–24.

Predation:
  Groupers seek nearest edible fish within ~170 units
  (guppy, goldfish, small angelfish).
  If distance < 28 and |Δz| < 0.18, prey.alive = false
  and grouper gets a short speed bump + 3–6.5s cooldown.

Flocks:
  1–2 flocks of 4–7 SMALL angelfish.
  Leader swims independently (arcs).
  Followers hold a triangle / V:
    row = (slot+2)//2, alternating sides,
    back = 28 + row*26, spread = 16 + row*14
    target = behind leader along heading, offset on perpendicular.
  Followers copy leader pitch and ease toward leader z.
  If the leader dies or leaves, promote the first living member.

Guarantees on randomize:
  At least one flock plus mixed loose fish including groupers
  and large angelfish.

================================================================
8. SCENERY (ALL PRESENT EVERY TANK)
================================================================
Always place ALL of the following together (not “one theme”):

8.1 Kelp / algae  (10–18 stalks)
    Base z fixed. Height 80–280.
    10 segments; p=0 at sand (rooted), p=1 at tip.
    Tip z waves toward/away from glass:
      z(p) = clamp(base_z + sin(...) * 0.16*p + ..., z_near, z_far)
    Lateral sway increases with p.
    Draw as polylines; each segment uses its own z for
    scale, parallax, and sort.

8.2 Rocks  (8–16)
    Varied width 28–150 * z_scale, irregular ellipses,
    different z and x along the sand.

8.3 Gems  (8–16)
    Diamonds on the sand, mixed z, gentle luma sparkle
    still clamped to 195.

8.4 Translucent-looking sculptures  (3–7)
    Gray mid-tone arches, obelisks, or spiral polylines
    at mixed z. Draw directly (no fullscreen alpha layer).

8.5 Pirate ship  (left side, z ≈ 0.62)
    Hull polygon, mast, waving sail, treasure chest + lid,
    two stick skeletons (skull, spine, arms, legs).

8.6 Castle  (right side, z ≈ 0.70)
    Keep, three towers, triangular roofs, merlons, dark gate
    with arched top.

8.7 Volcano  (center, cone z ≈ 0.78)
    Dark cone + crater.
    Particle fountain “lava”:
      Each bit: x,y,z, vx, vy, vz, life, radius.
      Spawn from crater. vy upward −220..−420, vx ±70,
      vz negative (−0.55..−0.18) so spray comes FORWARD
      toward the glass, then vz eases back; vy gets +280 gravity.
      Quiet periods spawn few bits; every few seconds a GUSH
      lasting 1.6–3.2s spawns ~18 bits/frame.
    Draw each bit with its own z (scale + parallax + sort
    among other world objects if practical; at minimum
    draw bits after the cone using each bit’s disparity).

8.8 Bubbles  (~28)
    Rise, slight sine drift, wrap at top. Gray ring circles.

Randomize (key X or startup) rebuilds fish, kelp, rocks,
gems, sculptures, bubbles, and resets volcano particles.
Ship/castle/volcano stay in their roles (left / right / center)
but the rest of the layout changes.

================================================================
9. FRAME LOOP
================================================================
1. Pump events (quit, resize, T, Y, X).
2. Update fish, flocks, predation, bubbles, volcano.
3. Remove dead/offscreen fish; spawn until target count.
4. If NORMAL: draw scene to the window, eye_sign=0.
   If anaglyph:
      draw scene into L with −disparity
      draw scene into R with +disparity
      optional swap L/R
      pack channels
      blit to window
5. flip display.

Draw scene:
  gradient water, sand, then all items far→near as in §5 and §8.

================================================================
10. WHAT NOT TO DO
================================================================
- No HUD text.
- No synthesized ambience, bubbles, or sine-wave sounds.
- No pygame._sdl2 for window position.
- No additive blend of SRCALPHA eye buffers onto the display.
- No saturated colors in NORMAL mode.
- No luma above 195 or below 36.
- Do not give far objects more stereo split than near ones.
- Do not skip z-sort.
- Do not implement only one of pirate / castle / volcano;
  all three belong in every tank.

================================================================
11. ACCEPTANCE
================================================================
A. Window opens, resizes, remembers size next launch.
B. Gray tank, muted grouper-like palette, no hot whites.
C. Fish coast unless they wag; paths curve; they pitch on
   climbs/dives; they change size as z changes.
D. Small angelfish travel in a V behind a leader.
E. Groupers eat small prey; population stays roughly constant.
F. Kelp tips sway in depth; bases stay planted.
G. Pirate ship left, castle right, volcano center.
H. Volcano periodically throws a large forward fountain.
I. T cycles gray / red-green / red-blue with no leftover tint
   when returning to gray.
J. Y swaps which color plate is left vs right.
K. Near fish show a wider red vs green/blue split than far fish.
L. --song plays looping music; without it the app is silent.
M. No on-screen text.

END OF SPEC